.TH kroppy 1
.SH NAME
kroppy, krop, krop-trimall \- a tool to crop PDF files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kroppy
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page briefly documents the
.B kroppy
command.
.B krop
and
.B krop-trimall
are the same program.
.PP
\fBkroppy\fP is a simple graphical tool to crop the pages of PDF files. It is written
in Python and relies on PyQt and PyMuPDF (or a suitable subset of pypdf/pikepdf/
python-poppler-qt) for its functionality.  A unique feature of kroppy is its
ability to automatically split pages into subpages to fit the limited screen
size of devices such as eReaders. This is particularly useful, if your eReader
does not support convenient scrolling.
.SH OPTIONS
A summary of options is included below.
For a complete description, use the \fB\-\-help\fP option.
.SS "Arguments:"
.TP
.B file
PDF file to open
.SS "Options:"
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
show help, including all options, and exit
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
show program's version number and exit
.TP
.B \-o OUTPUT, \-\-output OUTPUT
where to save the cropped PDF
.TP
.B \-\-whichpages WHICHPAGES
which pages (e.g. "1\-5" or "1,3\-") to include in cropped PDF (default: all)
.TP
.B \-\-rotate {0,90,180,270}
how much to rotate the cropped pdf clockwise (default: 0)
.TP
.B \-\-optimize {gs,no}
whether to optimize the final PDF using ghostscript (default: previous choice)
.TP
.B \-\-hard\-crop
hard-crop embedded images to the visible page box when saving, keeping their original encoding (default: previous choice, initially off)
.TP
.B \-\-grid GRID
if set to 2x3, for instance, creates a 2x3 grid of selections on initial page; if only one number is specified, the number of columns/rows is determined according to whether the page is landscape or portrait
.TP
.B \-\-initialpage INITIALPAGE
which page to open initially (default: 1)
.TP
.B \-\-selections {all,evenodd,individual}
to which pages should selections apply
.TP
.B \-\-exceptions EXCEPTIONS
pages (e.g. "1\-5" or "1,3\-") which require individual selections
.TP
.B \-\-trim
if specified, will auto trim initial selections
.TP
.B \-\-trim-use {initial,all}
whether to inspect only the initial page or all pages (slow!) when auto trimming (default: previous value)
.TP
.B \-\-trim\-padding TRIM_PADDING
how much padding to include when auto trimming (default: previous value)
.TP
.B \-\-log LOG
run log to append to, one flushed line per event. A path is always kept. "off" disables logging. By default the log is <input>.kroppy.log beside the PDF and is deleted when the session ends with no errors. $KROP_LOG is used when this option is omitted
.TP
.B \-\-log\-keep {always,on\-error,never}
always: keep the run log; on\-error: delete it when the session ends with no errors (default); never: do not write a run log (same as \-\-log off). Ignored when \-\-log names a file, which is always kept
.TP
.B \-\-log\-location {beside,central}
where an automatic run log is written: beside the PDF (default) or a central folder. Ignored when \-\-log names a file. Central logs older than 30 days are removed on startup
.TP
.B \-\-analyze\-only
print a per-page color and bit-depth recommendation and exit without opening the window
.TP
.B \-\-analyze\-json FILE
write the full analysis JSON to FILE and exit without opening the window
.TP
.B \-\-go
output PDF without opening the kroppy window (using the choices supplied on the command line); if used in a script without X server access, you can run kroppy using xvfb\-run
